      "characters": 16735,
      "head": "We are given a square $ABCD$ with side length 1, meaning all sides are length 1. The square is folded so that vertex $C$ meets edge $\\overline{AD}$ at $C'$, and edge $\\overline{BC}$ intersects edge $\\overline{AB}$ at point $E$. It is also given that $C'D = \\frac{1}{3}$. We are to find the **perimete",
      "tail": "} \\cdot \\frac{-5}{3} = -\\frac{4}{3}$\n\nSo equation is:\n$$\ny + \\frac{2}{15} = -\\frac{4}{3}(x - \\frac{3}{5})\n\\Rightarrow y = -\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{12}{15} - \\frac{2}{15} = -\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{10}{15} = -\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{2}{3}\n$$\n\nSet $y = 0$ (since we want intersection with $\\overline{AB}$):\n$$\n0 = -\\frac{4}{3}x + \\frac{2}{3} \\Rightarrow \\frac{4}{3}x = \\frac{2}{3} \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nSo point $E = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right)$\n\nNow we can compute lengths:\n\n- $AE = \\frac{1}{2}$\n- $EC' = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} - 0\\right)^2 + \\left(0 - \\frac{2}{3}\\right)^2} = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{4}{9}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{9 + 16}{36}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} = \\frac{5}{6}$\n- $AC' = \\frac{2}{3}$\n\nNow find perimeter:\n$$\n\\text{Perimeter} = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{5}{6} + \\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{3}{6} + \\frac{5}{6} + \\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{12}{6} = 2\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{2}\n$$\n\nAnswer: $2$"
